    },
    {
      "section_id": "SEC044",
      "title": "Flesh-and-Blood Knowledge",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "In Matthew chapter 16, Jesus himself asked, \"Who do men say that I the son of man am?\" And Peter answered, \"You are the Christ.\" Jesus then said that flesh and blood did not reveal this to Peter. There is, then, a flesh and blood revelation, and there is a revelation that does not come from flesh and blood but from God.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "IDEA170",
            "REF035",
            "SRC004629",
            "SRC004630",
            "SRC004635",
            "SRC004639",
            "SRC004640",
            "SRC004642",
            "SRC004645",
            "SRC004646",
            "SRC004648"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC004629",
            "SRC004630",
            "SRC004635",
            "SRC004639",
            "SRC004640",
            "SRC004642",
            "SRC004645",
            "SRC004646",
            "SRC004648"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [
            "IDEA170"
          ],
          "example_refs": [],
          "reference_refs": [
            "REF035"
          ],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000005",
          "provider_handle": "p5"
        },
        {
          "text": "That category of flesh and blood knowledge is still evident today, even in modern science. Doctors now use the heart of pigs and transplant it into a human cavity, and the person is alive. They use the liver of pigs, and the man is alive — the man lives. This is natural, flesh and blood knowledge, distinct from the revelation that comes only from God.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "IDEA170",
            "EX027",
            "SRC004654",
            "SRC004656",
            "SRC004657",
            "SRC004659",
            "SRC004661",
            "SRC004662"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC004654",
            "SRC004656",
            "SRC004657",
            "SRC004659",
            "SRC004661",
            "SRC004662",
            "SRC004630",
            "SRC004635",
            "SRC004639",
            "SRC004640",
            "SRC004642",
            "SRC004645",
            "SRC004646",
            "SRC004648"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [
            "IDEA170"
          ],
          "example_refs": [
            "EX027"
          ],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000006",
          "provider_handle": "p6"
        },
        {
          "text": "At the same time, believers must remain informed and relevant to their society rather than detached from the world's affairs in the name of spirituality. I don't listen to information or create some rule about it as a law, but you have to know where your people are. There is no use being someone who didn't listen to the news, asking where you want to live. You must be relevant to your people.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "IDEA171",
            "SRC004680",
            "SRC004682",
            "SRC004684",
            "SRC004687",
            "SRC004690",
            "SRC004692"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC004680",
            "SRC004682",
            "SRC004684",
            "SRC004687",
            "SRC004690",
            "SRC004692"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [
            "IDEA171"
          ],
          "example_refs": [],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000007",
          "provider_handle": "p7"
        },
        {
          "text": "Spiritual authority is undermined when leaders are irrelevant or ignorant of the practical concerns of the people they are sent to serve. For all the time I have known Paul Biya, I don't know of any discourse he made that did not address the economy. Every time he makes a speech or talks to the nation, I have been listening to him, and I can't remember one discourse he made that I didn't listen to. If you are sent by God and you don't know anything about the economy of the people you serve, you can see how relevant — or irrelevant — you really are.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "IDEA172",
            "EX028",
            "SRC004697",
            "SRC004702",
            "SRC004706",
            "SRC004722",
            "SRC004727",
            "SRC004729",
            "SRC004731",
            "SRC004734"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC004697",
            "SRC004702",
            "SRC004706",
            "SRC004722",
            "SRC004727",
            "SRC004729",
            "SRC004731",
            "SRC004734"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [
            "IDEA172"
          ],
          "example_refs": [
            "EX028"
          ],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000008",
          "provider_handle": "p8"
        }
      ],
